    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23308" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δακτῠλ-ιαῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of a finger's length, breadth</i> or <i>thickness,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥάβδοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Fract.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάραβοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					549b10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τομοὶ δ. τῷ τε μήκει καὶ πάχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Damocr.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.1000
			</span></i>: Astron., <i>a digit in extent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cleom.
				2.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>possessing</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκτυλοι, δ. μέρη τοῦ σώματος,</span>
			i.e. hands and feet, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.77
			</span></i>.</div>
